00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  football may be back but the looming  threat of omicron is undoing the premier  league schedule six out of ten matches  this weekend were cancelled and managers  now want a pause to the whole season  that's why i'm not against stopping the  league  i just don't see  the 100 benefit of it we think that we  should postpone the full round of  premier league games this weekend coming  up  the  the covet cases are going through the  roof in all the premier league clubs we  were just worried about the safety of  players the players were concerned about  their health because we had several  positive covey tests in several for in  consecutive days  despite the warnings after high-level  talks today the premier league decided  not to postpone the season you start to  look at the logistical nightmare in  terms of fixture congestion if games get  called off and there's no real guarantee  that this proposed circuit breaker and  indeed i i'm not certain that the  circuit breaker would have been  something that would have helped  um because you there's no guarantee that  in two weeks time or however long the  proposed circuit breaker was you'd be  out of this  but matches are already affected  tottenham's sunday game against  liverpool was their first in a fortnight  and where games do happen there are  warnings that healthy players are being  overused while others isolate pausing  the whole of the premier league would  have had huge implications this is a  busy schedule with very little slack  even moving matches by a week or two  would have been really hard to manage  not to mention the financial  implications that come with postponing  matches i think we're going to see  further games postponed and clearly that  that then has an impact on immediate  match day revenue and in some cases  possibly on broadcasting reviews if  there are a lot of if there's any long  breaks then new sponsors become  concerned because they're not getting  value for money from their sponsorship  as matches are moved across the english  game there has been criticism that not  enough players are vaccinated today the  bristol city squad were among those  taken for their boosters and we are a  long way from the empty stadiums of last  year there are currently 30 premier  league matches due to happen over  christmas in the new year  there is little consensus and festive  and football cheer is still at the mercy  of covid  ali forskew sky news

